<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-1478] Can&apos;t read spec compliant, 3-level lists via parquet-proto</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1478</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I noticed that ProtoInputOutputFormatTest doesn&apos;t test the following case properly: when lists are written using the spec compliant 3-level structure. The test actually doesn&apos;t write 3-level list, because the passed configuration is not used at all, a new one is created each time. See attached PR.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When I fixed this test, it turned out that it is failing: now it writes the correct 3-level structure, but looks like the read path is broken. Is it indeed a bug, or I&apos;m doing something wrong?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
